        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0620" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v13/pg590"/>

                <head>259. Memorandum of Conversation<anchor n="1" xml:id="d259-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1967-07-11T13:00:00-04:00"
                            >July 11, 1967, 1 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>
                        FRG Troop Levels; Chancellor Kiesinger’s Visit</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>PARTICIPANTS</label>
                    <item>President Johnson</item>
                    <item>
                        FRG Ambassador Knappstein
                    </item>
                    <item>Mr. Harry Obst, Language Services
                        (interpreter)</item>
                </list>
                <p>Ambassador Knappstein told the President
                    that he had a message which he had just received from Chancellor Kiesinger. The Chancellor <pb facs="0621"
                        n="591" xml:id="pg591"/> wanted the President to know that there has been no
                    decision to cut troop levels, just a reduction of the military budget in terms
                    of money. He wanted to assure the President that he will make no important
                    decisions on foreign policy without first consulting with the US. He accepts the
                    President’s invitation to come to Washington and accepts the dates of September
                    12–13. He would write the President a personal message the same day.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d259-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d259-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, DEF 6 GER W. Secret; Exdis. Drafted by
                    Obst and approved by the White House on July 13. The meeting was held at a
                    luncheon at the White House.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
